- Story & Context: Silas confesses to the crew that he has stopped digging for silver because the resonant frequency of his Minimoog creates ghost-maps of the tunnels on the stone ceilings that only he can decode. He stands amidst the damp granite, his hands slick with lubricating oil as he wrings a weeping, oscillating melody from his keyboard that sounds like water hitting lava. "My fingers leave a shadow where the vein used to sleep."
