Track 3: The Zenith-Corrosion Rhapsody
- Story & Context: After the mine was shuttered and filled with brackish water, legend tells of the "Zenith-Corrosion," a phenomenon where the abandoned ducting began to generate its own music without a human touch. Elara, the last guard to descend, swears she heard the pipes singing a hymn of salt and electricity, a sound that melted the rust from the air and turned the stagnant pool into a reflective mirror of the sky. "Let the pressure bloom into a crown of iron rust."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A dreamlike, surreal landscape image showing a flooded underground cathedral formed by collapsed mines, with rusted, twisted pipes rising from the dark water like church organ pillars, a massive circular optical atmospheric halo glowing in the distant darkness above, ethereal and haunting.

